WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.252
This table summarizes the text half of the module.

00:00:03.252 --> 00:00:07.342
Use the simplest function that matches the actual problem.

00:00:07.342 --> 00:00:10.892
Do not use regex when TRIM solves the issue.

00:00:10.892 --> 00:00:15.707
Do not use fixed positions when a reliable delimiter defines the structure.

00:00:15.707 --> 00:00:20.017
And do not treat cleaning as proof of validity.

00:00:20.017 --> 00:00:24.107
Clear, small transformations are easier to maintain and explain.

00:00:24.107 --> 00:00:29.597
Connect this idea to a hospital calculating length of stay and follow-up dates.

00:00:29.597 --> 00:00:35.402
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:43.202
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:43.202 --> 00:00:49.127
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:49.127 --> 00:00:55.156
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
